; An INLINE map carrying a group choice (`{ x: uint // y: tstr }`) used as a member/element type is
; rejected gracefully (`an inline map with group choices ... is unsupported`, parsing.rs
; `rust_type_from_type2`) — a DISTINCT arm from the one a choice-FREE inline map takes (`an inline
; map ... unsupported unless it is a table`): the group-choice count check trips first, so this
; fixture pins the multi-choice arm specifically. The named form (`t = { x: uint // y: tstr }`
; referenced by name) is the supported spelling, which the message points at. No matrix cell covers
; a group-choice map in member position (the contain.* map cells are choice-free), so this hand
; fixture is the pin. Surfaced by the recombination sweep (src/tests/recombination_tests.rs); the
; message itself is pinned by `inline_map_group_choice_member_rejects_gracefully`.
a = [{ x: uint // y: tstr }]
